<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="survey_instructions">
    <title>Survey Instructions</title>
    <shortdesc>Core Instructions for Logging in to Qualtrics for the First Time.</shortdesc>
    <taskbody>
        <context>Instructions for Logging in to<xref href="https://www.qualtrics.com/" format="html"
                scope="external"> Qualtrics</xref> for the First Time<p>Seeking feedback and upfront
                information about how a product or service is working - or is intended to work - can
                save hours of troubleshooting and service updates later. Creating a survey is quick
                and easy in Qualtrics.</p><p>While initial instructions differ by institutions for
                how to log in to Qualtrics, once logged in to the platform the overall procedure for
                developing a new survey is quick and easy. It does not differ by licensing
                institutions or authentication types.</p></context>
        <steps>
            <step>
                <cmd>From the landing page, click on "Create a Survey."</cmd>
                <info>
                    <p>
                        <fig id="fig_tw5_jb4_gfc">
                            <title>Qualtrics User Landing Page</title>
                            <image placement="break" href="../Anna/AnnaImage1.png" align="center"
                                id="image_uw5_jb4_gfc">
                                <alt>This image shows the Qualtrics User Landing Page.</alt>
                            </image>
                        </fig>
                    </p>
                </info>
            </step>
            <step>
                <cmd>The first time you log in as a new user, there will be a short user tour. Click
                    "next" at each stage (if applicable) to be introduced to a snapshot of this
                    guide.</cmd>
            </step>
            <step>
                <cmd>After completing the tour (if applicable), click on "Survey" under "From
                    Scratch." Then click "Get started.</cmd>
                <?Qualtrics will again offer an option for a user tour at this stage. Clicking through it may be additionally helpful. For the purposes of this guide, it is assumed that "Skip Tour" is selected.?>
                <info>
                    <p>
                        <fig id="fig_npf_nb4_gfc">
                            <title>The Create a New Survey From Scratch Option</title>
                            <image placement="break" href="../Anna/AnnaImage2.png" align="center"
                                id="image_opf_nb4_gfc">
                                <alt>An Image of How to Create a New Survey From Scratch. There are
                                    also drop-down options to import questions.</alt>
                            </image>
                        </fig>
                    </p>
                </info>
            </step>
            <step>
                <cmd>Give the project a title, and then click "Create Project."</cmd>
                <?It is also possible in Qualtrics to share surveys previously written by other users, or to import questions from a standardized user bank of user-submitted or proprietary questions that cover common use cases. It is also possible to save previously created questions that will be repeated multiple times (e.g. for longitudinal administrations of the same survey or for common questions such as demographics identifiers) in a personal library. Questions from these sources can be directly imported into a survey. To do so, select the appropriate choice from the dropdown menu and then navigate to where the intended question is located. Selecting a question from an external source will then make it the default first question in the new survey project just named in this step 3. This guide will only cover generating new questions from scratch in detail. Thus, the default selection for the dropdown box of "Create a Blank Survey Project" is assumed to be checked at this stage. ?>
                <info>
                    <p>
                        <fig id="fig_gqp_qb4_gfc">
                            <title>Creating a New Project</title>
                            <image placement="break" href="../Anna/AnnaImage3.png" align="center"
                                id="image_hqp_qb4_gfc">
                                <alt>More Detail of How to Create a New Project in Qualtrics.</alt>
                            </image>
                        </fig>
                    </p>
                </info>
            </step>
        </steps>
    </taskbody>
</task>
